# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map operator representations {#map-operator-representations}"
msgstr "オペレーター表現のマッピング {#map-operator-representations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Mappers** are routines that transform operators from one representation to another while preserving mathematical equivalence. Use them to work flexibly across different operator algebras and to prepare operators for quantum circuit execution.\n"
msgstr "**マッパー**は、数学的な等価性を保ったまま、オペレーターをある表現から別の表現へ変換するルーチンです。さまざまなオペレーター代数にまたがって柔軟に作業したり、量子回路の実行に向けてオペレーターを準備したりするために使います。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implement custom mappers {#implement-custom-mappers}"
msgstr "カスタム・マッパーの実装 {#implement-custom-mappers}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The mappers module makes it straightforward to implement custom mappings. Mappers work by transforming the fundamental actions (creation, annihilation, Majorana, and so on) that compose an operator, then combining these transformed actions according to the target representation’s rules.\n"
msgstr "マッパー・モジュールを使うと、カスタムのマッピングを簡単に実装できます。マッパーは、オペレーターを構成する基本的なアクション(生成、消滅、マヨラナなど)を変換し、変換後のアクションをターゲット表現の規則に従って組み合わせることで動作します。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a concrete example, consider a Jordan-Wigner transformation that maps a [`MajoranaOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-majorana-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.MajoranaOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.MajoranaOperator\") to a qubit operator using [`map_majorana_action_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-majorana-action-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_majorana_action_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_majorana_action_generators\"):\n"
msgstr "具体例として、[`map_majorana_action_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-majorana-action-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_majorana_action_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_majorana_action_generators\") を使って [`MajoranaOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-majorana-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.MajoranaOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.MajoranaOperator\") を量子ビット演算子に写像するJordan-Wigner変換を考えてみましょう。\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs group=\"code\">\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"PYTHON\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs group=\"code\">\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"PYTHON\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit.quantum_info import SparseObservable\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.mappers import map_majorana_action_generators\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators import MajoranaOperator\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Create a Majorana operator\n"
"    >>> maj_op = MajoranaOperator.from_dict({(0, 1): 1.0, (2,): 0.5})\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Define how each Majorana action maps to Pauli strings\n"
"    >>> num_qubits = 2\n"
"    >>> def map_action(mode: int) -> SparseObservable:\n"
"    ...     idx = mode // 2\n"
"    ...     qubits = list(range(idx + 1))\n"
"    ...     pauli = \"Y\" if mode % 2 else \"X\"\n"
"    ...     return SparseObservable.from_sparse_list(\n"
"    ...         [(\"Z\" * idx + pauli, qubits, 1.0)],\n"
"    ...         num_qubits=num_qubits,\n"
"    ...     )\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Apply the mapping to transform the operator\n"
"    >>> custom_observable = map_majorana_action_generators(\n"
"    ...     maj_op,\n"
"    ...     map_action,\n"
"    ...     identity=lambda: SparseObservable.identity(num_qubits),\n"
"    ...     compose=SparseObservable.compose,\n"
"    ... )\n"
"    >>> print(custom_observable.simplify())\n"
"    <SparseObservable with 2 terms on 2 qubits: (0+1j)(Z_0) + (0.5+0j)(X_1 Z_0)>\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <TabItem value=\"c\" label=\"C\">\n"
msgstr "  <TabItem value=\"c\" label=\"C\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    // The C API provides direct mapping functions for common transformations.\n"
"    // Custom mapper prototyping as shown in Python is primarily a Python feature.\n"
"    // For custom mappings in C, you will need to perform the iteration and\n"
"    // conversion logic entirely by yourself.\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The key steps to implement any custom mapper are:\n"
msgstr "カスタムマッパーを実装するための主な手順は次のとおりです。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Define action transformation**: Specify how each action (indexed by mode) maps to the target representation. In the example above, Majorana actions map to Pauli strings according to Jordan-Wigner rules.\n"
msgstr "**アクション変換を定義する**: 各アクション（モードでインデックス付けされたもの）が対象の表現へどのように写像されるかを指定します。上の例では、MajoranaアクションはJordan-Wignerの規則に従ってPauli文字列に写像されます。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Use one of the provided mapping functions**: The [`mappers`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers#module-qiskit_fermions.mappers \"qiskit_fermions.mappers\") module provides utility functions to handle iterating over the operator terms and subsequent applications of the custom action map for the operator representations provided by the [`operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") module. For example, [`map_majorana_action_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-majorana-action-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_majorana_action_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_majorana_action_generators\") works with Majorana operators.\n"
msgstr "**提供されているマッピング関数のいずれかを使う**: [`mappers`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers#module-qiskit_fermions.mappers \"qiskit_fermions.mappers\") モジュールには、[`operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") モジュールが提供する演算子表現について、演算子の項を反復処理し、カスタムのアクションマップを順に適用するためのユーティリティ関数が用意されています。たとえば、[`map_majorana_action_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-majorana-action-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_majorana_action_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_majorana_action_generators\") はMajorana演算子に対応しています。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Get the result**: The mapping function returns an operator in the target representation with the transformation applied consistently across all terms.\n"
msgstr "**結果を取得する**: マッピング関数は、すべての項に一貫して変換を適用した、対象の表現の演算子を返します。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This design makes it easy to prototype custom mappings without deep knowledge of internal operator structures. The transformation is applied automatically to every term in the operator while preserving mathematical equivalence.\n"
msgstr "この設計により、演算子の内部構造に深い知識がなくても、カスタムマッピングを簡単にプロトタイピングできます。変換は演算子のすべての項に自動的に適用され、数学的な等価性が保たれます。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Hint\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  You can also iterate the terms of an operator manually rather than using one of the provided iterator functions. See the section on [term iteration](operators#term-iteration-and-reconstruction) in the operators guide for details.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"ヒント\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  用意されているイテレーター関数を使わずに、演算子の項を手動で反復処理することもできます。詳細は、演算子ガイドの[項の反復処理](operators#term-iteration-and-reconstruction)のセクションを参照してください。\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Library implementations {#library-implementations}"
msgstr "ライブラリ実装 {#library-implementations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`qiskit_fermions.mappers.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library#module-qiskit_fermions.mappers.library \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library\") module provides efficient, thoroughly tested implementations of common mappings. These follow the same underlying pattern as custom mappers but are optimized for production use and are available in both the Python and C APIs.\n"
msgstr "[`qiskit_fermions.mappers.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library#module-qiskit_fermions.mappers.library \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library\") モジュールは、一般的なマッピングについて、効率的で十分にテストされた実装を提供します。これらはカスタムマッパーと同じ基本パターンに従いますが、本番利用向けに最適化されており、Python APIとC APIの両方で利用できます。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The example below applies a library mapper to the same [`MajoranaOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-majorana-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.MajoranaOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.MajoranaOperator\") from the custom mapper section, demonstrating equivalent results:\n"
msgstr "以下の例では、カスタムマッパーのセクションと同じ [`MajoranaOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-majorana-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.MajoranaOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.MajoranaOperator\") にライブラリのマッパーを適用し、同等の結果が得られることを示します。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.mappers.library import majorana_to_fermion, jordan_wigner\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Convert MajoranaOperator to FermionOperator using library mapper\n"
"    >>> ferm_op = majorana_to_fermion(maj_op)\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Apply Jordan-Wigner mapper to get qubit operator\n"
"    >>> sparse_observable = jordan_wigner(ferm_op, num_qubits=2)\n"
"    >>> difference = sparse_observable - custom_observable\n"
"    >>> print(difference.simplify() == SparseObservable.zero(num_qubits))\n"
"    True\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    #include <qiskit_fermions.h>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Create a MajoranaOperator with the same terms as maj_op above\n"
"    uint64_t num_terms = 2;\n"
"    uint64_t num_modes = 3;\n"
"    uint32_t modes[3] = {0, 1, 2};\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeffs[2] = {{1.0, 0.0}, {0.5, 0.0}};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries[3] = {0, 2, 3};\n"
"    QfMajoranaOperator *maj_op = qf_maj_op_new(num_terms, num_modes, coeffs, modes, boundaries);\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Create a MajoranaOperator with the same terms as maj_op above\n"
"    uint64_t num_terms = 2;\n"
"    uint64_t num_modes = 3;\n"
"    uint32_t modes[3] = {0, 1, 2};\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeffs[2] = {{1.0, 0.0}, {0.5, 0.0}};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries[3] = {0, 2, 3};\n"
"    QfMajoranaOperator *maj_op = qf_maj_op_new(num_terms, num_modes, coeffs, modes, boundaries);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Convert MajoranaOperator to FermionOperator using library mapper\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *ferm_op = qf_majorana_to_fermion(maj_op);\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Convert MajoranaOperator to FermionOperator using library mapper\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *ferm_op = qf_majorana_to_fermion(maj_op);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Apply Jordan-Wigner mapper to get qubit operator\n"
"    QkObs *qubit_op;\n"
"    QfExitCode exit = qf_ferm_op_jordan_wigner(ferm_op, 2, &qubit_op);\n"
"    assert(exit == QfExitCode_Success);\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Apply Jordan-Wigner mapper to get qubit operator\n"
"    QkObs *qubit_op;\n"
"    QfExitCode exit = qf_ferm_op_jordan_wigner(ferm_op, 2, &qubit_op);\n"
"    assert(exit == QfExitCode_Success);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Clean up\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_free(ferm_op);\n"
"    qf_maj_op_free(maj_op);\n"
"    qk_obs_free(qubit_op);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Clean up\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_free(ferm_op);\n"
"    qf_maj_op_free(maj_op);\n"
"    qk_obs_free(qubit_op);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The two-step above is written out to show two library mappers composing. In practice you would map a [`MajoranaOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-majorana-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.MajoranaOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.MajoranaOperator\") in one step instead, with [`majorana_jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-majorana-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.majorana_jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.majorana_jordan_wigner\") ([`qf_maj_op_jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions-c/qf-mappers-library#qf_maj_op_jordan_wigner \"qf_maj_op_jordan_wigner\") in the C API), and likewise for the other operator types – [`edge_vertex_jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-edge-vertex-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.edge_vertex_jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.edge_vertex_jordan_wigner\") and [`transfer_vertex_jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-transfer-vertex-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.transfer_vertex_jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.transfer_vertex_jordan_wigner\") ([`qf_edge_op_jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions-c/qf-mappers-library#qf_edge_op_jordan_wigner \"qf_edge_op_jordan_wigner\"), [`qf_transfer_op_jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions-c/qf-mappers-library#qf_transfer_op_jordan_wigner \"qf_transfer_op_jordan_wigner\")). Going via a [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") also inflates the intermediate result: every generator of these algebras maps onto a single Pauli string, whereas each fermionic action maps onto a two-term sum, so a term built from several generators expands only to be merged back down again. That saving grows with the length of the terms; for the single-generator terms of a hopping Hamiltonian the two routes cost about the same.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"注\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  上の2段階の手順は、2つのライブラリマッパーを組み合わせる様子を示すために書き出したものです。実際には、[`MajoranaOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-majorana-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.MajoranaOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.MajoranaOperator\") は [`majorana_jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-majorana-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.majorana_jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.majorana_jordan_wigner\")（C APIでは [`qf_maj_op_jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions-c/qf-mappers-library#qf_maj_op_jordan_wigner \"qf_maj_op_jordan_wigner\")）を使って1ステップで写像します。他の演算子タイプについても同様で、[`edge_vertex_jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-edge-vertex-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.edge_vertex_jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.edge_vertex_jordan_wigner\") と [`transfer_vertex_jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-transfer-vertex-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.transfer_vertex_jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.transfer_vertex_jordan_wigner\")（[`qf_edge_op_jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions-c/qf-mappers-library#qf_edge_op_jordan_wigner \"qf_edge_op_jordan_wigner\")、[`qf_transfer_op_jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions-c/qf-mappers-library#qf_transfer_op_jordan_wigner \"qf_transfer_op_jordan_wigner\")）があります。[`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") を経由すると中間結果も膨らみます。これらの代数のすべての生成子は単一のPauli文字列に写像されるのに対し、各フェルミオンアクションは2項の和に写像されるため、複数の生成子から成る項は展開されたのち、再び統合されることになります。この節約効果は項が長くなるほど大きくなり、ホッピングハミルトニアンのような単一生成子の項では、2つの経路のコストはほぼ同じです。\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the Python API, some of these library mappers are also reachable through type-agnostic convenience mappers. [`fermion_operator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.fermion_operator \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.fermion_operator\") and [`majorana_operator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-majorana-operator#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.majorana_operator \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.majorana_operator\") sit in front of [`majorana_to_fermion()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-majorana-to-fermion#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.majorana_to_fermion \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.majorana_to_fermion\") and [`fermion_to_majorana()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-fermion-to-majorana#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.fermion_to_majorana \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.fermion_to_majorana\") (among others), delegating to the appropriate library implementation internally based on the type of object they are given, rather than requiring you to pick the right function yourself. The same applies to [`jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner\") and to [`ternary_tree()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-ternary-tree#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.ternary_tree \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.ternary_tree\") (introduced below), each of which dispatches to whichever direct implementation matches the operator it is given. See [`qiskit_fermions.protocols`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/protocols#module-qiskit_fermions.protocols \"qiskit_fermions.protocols\") for how this dispatch is implemented internally.\n"
msgstr "Python APIでは、これらのライブラリマッパーの一部は、型に依存しない便利なマッパーからも利用できます。[`fermion_operator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.fermion_operator \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.fermion_operator\") と [`majorana_operator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-majorana-operator#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.majorana_operator \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.majorana_operator\") は、[`majorana_to_fermion()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-majorana-to-fermion#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.majorana_to_fermion \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.majorana_to_fermion\") や [`fermion_to_majorana()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-fermion-to-majorana#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.fermion_to_majorana \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.fermion_to_majorana\")（ほか）の前段に位置し、渡されたオブジェクトの型に基づいて内部で適切なライブラリ実装に処理を委ねるため、適切な関数を自分で選ぶ必要がありません。同じことが [`jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner\") と（後述の）[`ternary_tree()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-ternary-tree#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.ternary_tree \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.ternary_tree\") にも当てはまり、それぞれ、渡された演算子に対応する直接の実装へ振り分けます。この振り分けが内部でどのように実装されているかについては、[`qiskit_fermions.protocols`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/protocols#module-qiskit_fermions.protocols \"qiskit_fermions.protocols\") を参照してください。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose an encoding with ternary trees {#choose-an-encoding-with-ternary-trees}"
msgstr "三分木でエンコーディングを選ぶ {#choose-an-encoding-with-ternary-trees}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Jordan-Wigner is not the only fermion-to-qubit encoding, and it is not the cheapest. Its $Z$ strings grow with the mode index, so a Majorana operator on the last of $n$ modes maps onto a Pauli string of weight $n$. Encodings that spread the parity information across a tree instead of a chain do asymptotically better.\n"
msgstr "Jordan-Wignerはフェルミオンから量子ビットへの唯一のエンコーディングではなく、最も低コストというわけでもありません。その $Z$ 文字列はモードのインデックスとともに長くなるため、$n$ 個のモードの最後にあるMajorana演算子は、重み $n$ のPauli文字列に写像されます。パリティ情報を鎖ではなく木に分散させるエンコーディングは、漸近的により優れた性能を示します。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **ternary tree** on $n$ nodes captures this whole family. Each node is a qubit carrying three downward links labeled `X`, `Y` and `Z`; a link either descends to a child node (an *edge*) or terminates (a *leg*). Each leg’s path back to the root spells a Pauli string: crossing the link labeled $P$ that descends *from* node $u$ contributes $P$ on qubit $u$. Every such tree yields a valid encoding, and the familiar ones are simply particular shapes – a chain along `Z` is Jordan-Wigner, while a tree in which every node has three children, as far as the node count allows, is balanced.\n"
msgstr "$n$ 個のノードをもつ**三分木**は、この一族全体を捉えます。各ノードは `X`、`Y`、`Z` とラベル付けされた3本の下向きのリンクをもつ量子ビットです。リンクは子ノードへ降りるか（*辺*）、終端になるか（*葉*）のいずれかです。各葉からルートへ戻る経路はPauli文字列を表します。ノード $u$ から降りるラベル $P$ のリンクをたどると、量子ビット $u$ 上の $P$ が寄与します。どの木も有効なエンコーディングを与え、よく知られたものは特定の形にすぎません。`Z` に沿った鎖はJordan-Wignerであり、ノード数が許す限りすべてのノードが3つの子をもつ木は平衡木です。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.mappers import TernaryTree, TernaryTreeEncoding\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Jordan-Wigner is a chain descending along Z, with X and Y as legs at every node.\n"
"    >>> TernaryTree.chain(13, \"Z\").max_weight\n"
"    13\n"
"    >>> # The balanced tree spreads the same information over depth log_3(2n+1).\n"
"    >>> TernaryTree.breadth_first(13, 3).max_weight\n"
"    3\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    QfTernaryTree *chain;\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_chain(13, QfPauliLabel_Z, &chain);\n"
msgstr ""
"    QfTernaryTree *chain;\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_chain(13, QfPauliLabel_Z, &chain);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    QfPauliLabel order[3] = {QfPauliLabel_X, QfPauliLabel_Y, QfPauliLabel_Z};\n"
"    QfTernaryTree *balanced;\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_breadth_first(13, 3, order, &balanced);\n"
msgstr ""
"    QfPauliLabel order[3] = {QfPauliLabel_X, QfPauliLabel_Y, QfPauliLabel_Z};\n"
"    QfTernaryTree *balanced;\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_breadth_first(13, 3, order, &balanced);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    assert(qf_ternary_tree_max_weight(chain) == 13);\n"
"    assert(qf_ternary_tree_max_weight(balanced) == 3);\n"
msgstr ""
"    assert(qf_ternary_tree_max_weight(chain) == 13);\n"
"    assert(qf_ternary_tree_max_weight(balanced) == 3);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    qf_ternary_tree_free(chain);\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_free(balanced);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    qf_ternary_tree_free(chain);\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_free(balanced);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That maximum weight is optimal. [Jiang et al.](https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.10746) prove that the Majorana operators of *any* fermion-to-qubit mapping of $n$ modes have an average Pauli weight of at least $\\log_3(2n)$, so no mapping can bring the largest of them below $\\lceil \\log_3(2n+1) \\rceil$. Both trees use exactly $n$ qubits, so the saving is in Pauli weight, not qubit count.\n"
msgstr "この最大重みは最適です。[Jiang et al.](https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.10746) は、$n$ 個のモードに対する*あらゆる*フェルミオンから量子ビットへのマッピングのMajorana演算子は、平均Pauli重みが少なくとも $\\log_3(2n)$ であることを証明しており、したがって最大のものを $\\lceil \\log_3(2n+1) \\rceil$ 未満にできるマッピングは存在しません。どちらの木もちょうど $n$ 個の量子ビットを使うため、節約されるのは量子ビット数ではなくPauli重みです。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To map an operator, compile a tree into an encoding and hand that to a mapper along with the qubit count for the result. Compiling pairs the tree’s legs into Majorana operators and builds their Pauli strings once, so the same encoding should be reused across many operators. The qubit count stays with the mapping call rather than the encoding, so one encoding can serve registers of different widths; a count above the tree’s node count pads with the identity.\n"
msgstr "演算子を写像するには、木をエンコーディングにコンパイルし、結果の量子ビット数とともにマッパーに渡します。コンパイルでは、木の葉をMajorana演算子として対にし、それらのPauli文字列を一度だけ構築するため、同じエンコーディングを多数の演算子で再利用してください。量子ビット数はエンコーディングではなくマッピング呼び出し側で指定するため、1つのエンコーディングで異なる幅のレジスタに対応できます。木のノード数を超える量子ビット数を指定した場合は、恒等演算子で埋められます。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.mappers.library import fermion_ternary_tree\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators import FermionOperator\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> hamiltonian = FermionOperator.from_dict(\n"
"    ...     {((True, 0), (False, 3)): 1.0, ((True, 3), (False, 0)): 1.0}\n"
"    ... )\n"
"    >>> encoding = TernaryTreeEncoding(TernaryTree.breadth_first(4, 3))\n"
"    >>> fermion_ternary_tree(hamiltonian, encoding, 4).simplify()\n"
"    <SparseObservable with 2 terms on 4 qubits: (0.5+0j)(Y_3 Z_1 Y_0) + (0.5+0j)(X_3 Z_2 X_0)>\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    // Create the hopping Hamiltonian a^dagger_0 a_3 + a^dagger_3 a_0\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *hamiltonian = qf_ferm_op_zero();\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeffs[2] = {{1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    bool actions[4] = {true, false, true, false};\n"
"    uint32_t indices[4] = {0, 3, 3, 0};\n"
"    for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {\n"
"        qf_ferm_op_add_term(hamiltonian, 2, actions + 2 * i, indices + 2 * i, &coeffs[i]);\n"
"    }\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    QfPauliLabel order[3] = {QfPauliLabel_X, QfPauliLabel_Y, QfPauliLabel_Z};\n"
"    QfTernaryTree *tree;\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_breadth_first(4, 3, order, &tree);\n"
msgstr ""
"    QfPauliLabel order[3] = {QfPauliLabel_X, QfPauliLabel_Y, QfPauliLabel_Z};\n"
"    QfTernaryTree *tree;\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_breadth_first(4, 3, order, &tree);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Compile the tree once, then reuse the encoding for every operator mapped through it.\n"
"    QfTernaryTreeEncoding *encoding;\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_encoding_new(tree, NULL, &encoding);\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Compile the tree once, then reuse the encoding for every operator mapped through it.\n"
"    QfTernaryTreeEncoding *encoding;\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_encoding_new(tree, NULL, &encoding);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    QkObs *qubit_op;\n"
"    QfExitCode exit = qf_ferm_op_ternary_tree(hamiltonian, encoding, 4, &qubit_op);\n"
"    assert(exit == QfExitCode_Success);\n"
msgstr ""
"    QkObs *qubit_op;\n"
"    QfExitCode exit = qf_ferm_op_ternary_tree(hamiltonian, encoding, 4, &qubit_op);\n"
"    assert(exit == QfExitCode_Success);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Clean up\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_free(hamiltonian);\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_encoding_free(encoding);\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_free(tree);\n"
"    qk_obs_free(qubit_op);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Clean up\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_free(hamiltonian);\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_encoding_free(encoding);\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_free(tree);\n"
"    qk_obs_free(qubit_op);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mapping through a chain along `Z` reproduces [`fermion_jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-fermion-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.fermion_jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.fermion_jordan_wigner\") ([`qf_ferm_op_jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions-c/qf-mappers-library#qf_ferm_op_jordan_wigner \"qf_ferm_op_jordan_wigner\") in the C API) exactly, which is the sense in which this generalizes it:\n"
msgstr "`Z` に沿った鎖を通したマッピングは、[`fermion_jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-fermion-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.fermion_jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.fermion_jordan_wigner\")（C APIでは [`qf_ferm_op_jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions-c/qf-mappers-library#qf_ferm_op_jordan_wigner \"qf_ferm_op_jordan_wigner\")）をそのまま再現します。これが、このエンコーディングがJordan-Wignerを一般化しているという意味です。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every operator representation has a ternary-tree mapper, mirroring the Jordan-Wigner set; see [`qiskit_fermions.mappers.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library#module-qiskit_fermions.mappers.library \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library\") for the full list, and [Mapper Library](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions-c/qf-mappers-library#qf-mapper-library) in the C API. In the Python API they are also reachable through [`ternary_tree()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-ternary-tree#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.ternary_tree \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.ternary_tree\"), the type-agnostic wrapper that picks the right one for the operator it is given, just as [`jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner\") does:\n"
msgstr "すべての演算子表現には、Jordan-Wignerのセットに対応する三分木マッパーがあります。完全な一覧は [`qiskit_fermions.mappers.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library#module-qiskit_fermions.mappers.library \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library\") を、C APIについては [Mapper Library](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions-c/qf-mappers-library#qf-mapper-library) を参照してください。Python APIでは、[`jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner\") と同様に、渡された演算子に適したものを選ぶ型非依存のラッパーである [`ternary_tree()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-ternary-tree#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.ternary_tree \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.ternary_tree\") からも利用できます。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Some identities that hold under Jordan-Wigner are properties of the *chain* rather than of ternary trees. The number operator is $n_j = (1 - Z_j)/2$ only on the chain; on another tree the $Z_j$ becomes a $Z$ string over a set of qubits. Likewise a vertex operator $V_j$ is the weight-1 Pauli $Z_j$ only on the chain, where the two Majorana strings’ $Z$ chains cancel.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"注\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Jordan-Wignerで成り立つ恒等式の中には、三分木一般ではなく*鎖*に固有の性質であるものがあります。数演算子が $n_j = (1 - Z_j)/2$ となるのは鎖の場合だけで、他の木では $Z_j$ は量子ビットの集合にわたる $Z$ 文字列になります。同様に、頂点演算子 $V_j$ が重み1のPauli $Z_j$ になるのも鎖の場合だけで、そこでは2つのMajorana文字列の $Z$ 鎖が打ち消し合います。\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because every number operator still maps to a single $Z$ string, a Fock state is still a computational basis state under any ternary tree, but bit $q$ no longer reads occupation $q$. Occupation $j$ is instead the parity of the measured bits on the support of $n_j$’s image. Read those supports off the mapper rather than deriving them from the tree, so the decoding stays correct for any shape or mode permutation:\n"
msgstr "すべての数演算子は依然として単一の $Z$ 文字列に写像されるため、どの三分木でもFock状態は計算基底状態のままですが、ビット $q$ はもはや占有数 $q$ を表しません。占有数 $j$ は、代わりに $n_j$ の像の台に含まれる測定ビットのパリティになります。デコードがどんな形やモードの置換に対しても正しく保たれるよう、これらの台は木から導出するのではなく、マッパーから読み取ってください。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On this balanced tree, mode 0 is occupied when qubits 0, 1, and 2 hold an odd number of ones, so preparing it means flipping qubit 0 alone, while decoding a measured bitstring takes the parity over all three. A single bit-flip error on qubit 1 then corrupts the occupations of both mode 0 and mode 1, which matters for any workflow that reads occupations from noisy samples.\n"
msgstr "この平衡木では、量子ビット0、1、2に含まれる1の数が奇数のときにモード0が占有されます。したがって、これを準備するには量子ビット0だけを反転させればよい一方、測定したビット列をデコードするには3つすべてのパリティを取る必要があります。量子ビット1での単一のビット反転エラーは、モード0とモード1の両方の占有数を壊すため、ノイズのあるサンプルから占有数を読み取るワークフローでは問題になります。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") is lowered through such a mapper, wrap the mapper in [`group_wise()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-group-wise#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise\") (see [Synthesize an Evolution gate in fermionic space](fermionic-synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation)). A hopping term maps to two commuting Pauli strings, neither of which conserves particle number on its own; only their product in the evolution does. Under Jordan-Wigner both strings act on the same qubits, so a simplified term order keeps them adjacent. Under other trees their supports differ (as in `Y_3 Z_1 Y_0` and `X_3 Z_2 X_0` earlier), the raw and the simplified orders both interleave them with the images of other terms, and a qubit-side product formula then leaks particle number.\n"
msgstr "[`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") をこのようなマッパーで下位化する場合は、マッパーを [`group_wise()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-group-wise#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise\") でラップしてください（[フェルミオン空間でのEvolutionゲートの合成](fermionic-synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation)を参照）。ホッピング項は2つの可換なPauli文字列に写像され、どちらも単独では粒子数を保存せず、保存されるのは進化におけるそれらの積だけです。Jordan-Wignerでは両方の文字列が同じ量子ビットに作用するため、簡約された項の順序によって両者が隣り合ったままになります。他の木では（前述の `Y_3 Z_1 Y_0` と `X_3 Z_2 X_0` のように）台が異なり、元の順序でも簡約後の順序でも他の項の像がそれらの間に挟まるため、量子ビット側の積公式では粒子数が漏れ出してしまいます。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build an arbitrary tree {#build-an-arbitrary-tree}"
msgstr "任意の木を構築する {#build-an-arbitrary-tree}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The chain and breadth-first constructors cover the uniform families, but the general interface takes one `(parent, label)` pair per node, with `None` for the root (the C API takes the root’s index instead). This matters because the trees worth searching for are usually neither a chain nor uniform – the Bonsai algorithm, for instance, grows a spanning tree of a device’s coupling graph, so its branching follows that connectivity.\n"
msgstr "鎖と幅優先のコンストラクターは一様な族を扱いますが、一般的なインターフェースでは、ノードごとに1組の `(parent, label)` を受け取り、ルートには `None` を指定します（C APIではルートのインデックスを受け取ります）。探す価値のある木は、たいてい鎖でも一様でもないため、これは重要です。たとえばBonsaiアルゴリズムは、デバイスの結合グラフの全域木を成長させるため、その分岐はその接続性に従います。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> # Node 0 branches three ways, node 1 twice, and node 4 carries a single child.\n"
"    >>> tree = TernaryTree([None, (0, \"X\"), (0, \"Y\"), (0, \"Z\"), (1, \"X\"), (1, \"Z\"), (4, \"Y\")])\n"
"    >>> tree.num_nodes, tree.num_legs, tree.max_weight\n"
"    (7, 15, 4)\n"
"    >>> tree.children(0)\n"
"    {'X': 1, 'Y': 2, 'Z': 3}\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    // Node 0, the root, branches three ways, node 1 twice, and node 4 carries a single child.\n"
"    // The root has no parent and no incoming link, so its entries are never read: any value works.\n"
"    #define IGNORED 0\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    uint32_t parents[7] = {IGNORED, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 4};\n"
"    QfPauliLabel labels[7] = {\n"
"        IGNORED,        QfPauliLabel_X, QfPauliLabel_Y, QfPauliLabel_Z,\n"
"        QfPauliLabel_X, QfPauliLabel_Z, QfPauliLabel_Y,\n"
"    };\n"
msgstr ""
"    uint32_t parents[7] = {IGNORED, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 4};\n"
"    QfPauliLabel labels[7] = {\n"
"        IGNORED,        QfPauliLabel_X, QfPauliLabel_Y, QfPauliLabel_Z,\n"
"        QfPauliLabel_X, QfPauliLabel_Z, QfPauliLabel_Y,\n"
"    };\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    QfTernaryTree *tree;\n"
"    QfExitCode exit = qf_ternary_tree_new(7, 0, parents, labels, &tree);\n"
"    assert(exit == QfExitCode_Success);\n"
msgstr ""
"    QfTernaryTree *tree;\n"
"    QfExitCode exit = qf_ternary_tree_new(7, 0, parents, labels, &tree);\n"
"    assert(exit == QfExitCode_Success);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    assert(qf_ternary_tree_num_nodes(tree) == 7);\n"
"    assert(qf_ternary_tree_num_legs(tree) == 15);\n"
"    assert(qf_ternary_tree_max_weight(tree) == 4);\n"
msgstr ""
"    assert(qf_ternary_tree_num_nodes(tree) == 7);\n"
"    assert(qf_ternary_tree_num_legs(tree) == 15);\n"
"    assert(qf_ternary_tree_max_weight(tree) == 4);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    qf_ternary_tree_free(tree);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    qf_ternary_tree_free(tree);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note the leg count: it is always $2n+1$, whatever the shape. A node with fewer children does not generate fewer Pauli strings – its unused links are legs, and a leg spells a string just as an edge’s descendants do. Of those $2n+1$ strings, $2n$ pair into the Majorana operators of the $n$ modes, and exactly one is left over.\n"
msgstr "葉の数に注目してください。形に関わらず、常に $2n+1$ です。子の少ないノードが生成するPauli文字列が少なくなるわけではありません。使われないリンクは葉になり、葉は辺の子孫と同じようにPauli文字列を表します。これら $2n+1$ 個の文字列のうち、$2n$ 個は $n$ 個のモードのMajorana演算子として対になり、ちょうど1つが余ります。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Total parity {#total-parity}"
msgstr "全パリティ {#total-parity}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That leftover leg is the total fermionic parity $\\prod_j (1 - 2 n_j)$. It is a property of the encoding rather than a mapping of any operator, so it is a method on the encoding itself:\n"
msgstr "その余った葉が、全フェルミオンパリティ $\\prod_j (1 - 2 n_j)$ です。これは演算子のマッピングではなくエンコーディングの性質であるため、エンコーディング自体のメソッドになっています。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> TernaryTreeEncoding(TernaryTree.chain(4, \"Z\")).total_parity(4)\n"
"    <SparseObservable with 1 term on 4 qubits: (1+0j)(Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0)>\n"
"    >>> TernaryTreeEncoding(TernaryTree.breadth_first(4, 3)).total_parity(4)\n"
"    <SparseObservable with 1 term on 4 qubits: (1+0j)(Z_3 Z_0)>\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    QfTernaryTree *tree;\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_chain(4, QfPauliLabel_Z, &tree);\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    QfTernaryTreeEncoding *encoding;\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_encoding_new(tree, NULL, &encoding);\n"
msgstr ""
"    QfTernaryTreeEncoding *encoding;\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_encoding_new(tree, NULL, &encoding);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // On the chain this is the full Z string; on the balanced tree it is not.\n"
"    QkObs *parity;\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_encoding_total_parity(encoding, 4, &parity);\n"
msgstr ""
"    // On the chain this is the full Z string; on the balanced tree it is not.\n"
"    QkObs *parity;\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_encoding_total_parity(encoding, 4, &parity);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    qf_ternary_tree_encoding_free(encoding);\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_free(tree);\n"
"    qk_obs_free(parity);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    qf_ternary_tree_encoding_free(encoding);\n"
"    qf_ternary_tree_free(tree);\n"
"    qk_obs_free(parity);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As the balanced case shows, this is *not* in general the all-$Z$ string: it is the leg reached by the all-$Z$ *path*, which acts as the identity on every node not on that path.\n"
msgstr "平衡木の場合が示すように、これは一般にすべてが $Z$ の文字列では*ありません*。すべてが $Z$ の*経路*でたどり着く葉であり、その経路上にないすべてのノードでは恒等演算子として作用します。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Total parity here is an **observable to measure, not a constraint to impose**. Both of its eigenvalues are physical, so do not project a state onto the $+1$ sector: a ternary-tree encoding spends one qubit per mode and is onto the full $2^n$-dimensional space, leaving no unphysical subspace to project away.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"重要\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  ここでの全パリティは、**課す制約ではなく、測定する観測量**です。2つの固有値はどちらも物理的であるため、状態を $+1$ セクターに射影しないでください。三分木エンコーディングはモードごとに量子ビットを1つ使い、$2^n$ 次元の空間全体への全射であるため、射影して取り除くべき非物理的な部分空間は残りません。\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"bravyi-kitaev-by-hand\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Worked example: a Bravyi-Kitaev tree {#worked-example-a-bravyi-kitaev-tree}"
msgstr "実例: Bravyi-Kitaev木 {#worked-example-a-bravyi-kitaev-tree}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specifications are more often computed than typed out, since the tree for a real encoding is rarely small enough to write by hand. Bravyi-Kitaev is a good example: it belongs to this family, but its tree is not uniform, so no convenience constructor covers it.\n"
msgstr "実際のエンコーディングの木は手で書き出せるほど小さいことがまれなため、仕様は手入力するよりも計算で求めることのほうが多くなります。Bravyi-Kitaevは良い例です。この族に属していますが、その木は一様ではないため、便利なコンストラクターではカバーできません。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Its tree is built by a recursive split over the nodes, one per mode. Within a range of nodes $[l, r]$, let $h$ be the largest power of two that fits; the node placed for that range is $l + h - 1$, the last one in that block. Its `X` link descends to the tree built from the block before it and its `Z` link to the tree built from the remainder after it, leaving its `Y` link as a leg:\n"
msgstr "その木は、モードごとに1つずつあるノードに対する再帰的な分割によって構築されます。ノードの範囲 $[l, r]$ の中で、収まる最大の2の冪を $h$ とすると、その範囲に置かれるノードはそのブロックの最後である $l + h - 1$ です。その `X` リンクは、手前のブロックから構築された木へ降り、`Z` リンクは、後ろに残った部分から構築された木へ降り、`Y` リンクは葉として残ります。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At four modes the whole range is a single block, so the node placed first is 3, with $[0, 2]$ before it and nothing after; that sub-range gives node 1 over the single nodes 0 and 2. Compiling the tree confirms the encoding is Bravyi-Kitaev and not merely a tree of the same shape class – its first Majorana image is $X_0 X_1 X_3$:\n"
msgstr "4モードでは範囲全体が1つのブロックなので、最初に置かれるノードは3であり、その前に $[0, 2]$ があり、後ろには何もありません。この部分範囲からは、単一のノード0と2の上にノード1が置かれます。木をコンパイルすると、このエンコーディングが同じ形のクラスの木にとどまらず、確かにBravyi-Kitaevであることが確認できます。最初のMajorana像は $X_0 X_1 X_3$ です。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Its total parity makes the point of the previous section concrete: the leftover leg is the one reached by the all-$Z$ path, and here that path stops at the root, so the observable is the single-qubit $Z_3$ rather than a string over all four qubits:\n"
msgstr "その全パリティは、前のセクションの要点を具体的に示しています。余った葉はすべてが $Z$ の経路でたどり着く葉であり、ここではその経路がルートで止まるため、観測量は4つの量子ビットすべてにわたる文字列ではなく、単一量子ビットの $Z_3$ になります。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Scaling up needs nothing but a larger argument. Because no node ever spends its `Y` link on an edge, each branches at most two ways, so the Pauli weight grows logarithmically rather than linearly:\n"
msgstr "規模を大きくするのに必要なのは、より大きな引数だけです。どのノードも `Y` リンクを辺に使わないため、各ノードは最大で2方向にしか分岐せず、Pauli重みは線形ではなく対数的に増加します。\n"
